1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:02,138
On the first night

2
00:00:02,138 --> 00:00:03,077
of the Quiet,

3
00:00:03,077 --> 00:00:03,976
two of them stood

4
00:00:03,976 --> 00:00:04,751
at the edge of

5
00:00:04,751 --> 00:00:05,527
the trees.

6
00:00:05,527 --> 00:00:06,549
Perfectly still.

7
00:00:06,549 --> 00:00:07,774
Watching our window.

8
00:00:12,874 --> 00:00:14,266
My name is Noah.

9
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:15,349
I'm fifteen.

10
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:16,638
This is my grandpa's

11
00:00:16,638 --> 00:00:18,339
cabin on Kestrel Lake,

12
00:00:18,339 --> 00:00:19,731
about forty miles from

13
00:00:19,731 --> 00:00:21,382
anything with a name.

14
00:00:22,282 --> 00:00:23,454
That's my sister,

15
00:00:23,454 --> 00:00:24,018
June.

16
00:00:24,018 --> 00:00:24,928
She's eight.

17
00:00:24,928 --> 00:00:26,187
And that's Biscuit.

18
00:00:26,187 --> 00:00:27,228
He's a beagle,

19
00:00:27,228 --> 00:00:28,356
and he's twelve,

20
00:00:28,356 --> 00:00:29,353
which in dog years

21
00:00:29,353 --> 00:00:30,481
means he's allowed to

22
00:00:30,481 --> 00:00:31,522
sleep all day.

23
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:33,359
Three days ago,

24
00:00:33,359 --> 00:00:34,478
the blizzard hit.

25
00:00:34,478 --> 00:00:35,722
The power went out.

26
00:00:35,722 --> 00:00:37,049
The phones went dead.

27
00:00:37,049 --> 00:00:38,128
And the radio...

28
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:38,915
just hiss.

29
00:00:40,015 --> 00:00:41,176
Grandpa said not to

30
00:00:41,176 --> 00:00:41,854
worry.

31
00:00:41,854 --> 00:00:42,968
He dragged the old

32
00:00:42,968 --> 00:00:44,323
generator into the shed

33
00:00:44,323 --> 00:00:45,774
and got it running.

34
00:00:45,774 --> 00:00:46,838
That hum has been

35
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:47,951
the only sound out

36
00:00:47,951 --> 00:00:49,210
here ever since.

37
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:51,380
Then this morning,

38
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:52,508
Grandpa was gone.

39
00:00:52,508 --> 00:00:53,970
His snowmobile was gone.

40
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:55,140
And on the table,

41
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,185
there was this.

42
00:00:57,085 --> 00:00:58,084
Gone for help.

43
00:00:58,084 --> 00:00:59,206
Head is pounding.

44
00:00:59,206 --> 00:01:00,204
Something is in the

45
00:01:00,204 --> 00:01:00,703
air.

46
00:01:00,703 --> 00:01:01,908
Keep the windows...

47
00:01:01,908 --> 00:01:02,990
and that's where June

48
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:04,155
spilled her cocoa.

49
00:01:04,155 --> 00:01:05,111
I'm pretty sure it

50
00:01:05,111 --> 00:01:05,900
says shut.

51
00:01:07,001 --> 00:01:08,079
Something is in the

52
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:08,618
air.

53
00:01:08,618 --> 00:01:09,742
So whatever took the

54
00:01:09,742 --> 00:01:10,686
sound out of the

55
00:01:10,686 --> 00:01:11,406
world...

56
00:01:11,406 --> 00:01:12,305
is outside.

57
00:01:12,305 --> 00:01:13,519
Breathing the same air

58
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:14,239
we are.

59
00:01:15,239 --> 00:01:16,066
So I did what

60
00:01:16,066 --> 00:01:17,308
Grandpa would do.

61
00:01:17,308 --> 00:01:18,365
I made rules.

62
00:01:19,665 --> 00:01:20,412
Rule one.

63
00:01:20,412 --> 00:01:21,656
Keep the hum going.

64
00:01:21,656 --> 00:01:22,650
The hum means we're

65
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:23,188
okay.

66
00:01:24,888 --> 00:01:25,641
Rule two.

67
00:01:25,641 --> 00:01:27,061
Keep every window shut.

68
00:01:27,382 --> 00:01:28,189
But it's so stuffy

69
00:01:28,189 --> 00:01:28,787
in here.

70
00:01:29,108 --> 00:01:29,808
Rule two,

71
00:01:29,808 --> 00:01:30,313
June.

72
00:01:32,013 --> 00:01:32,822
Rule three.

73
00:01:32,822 --> 00:01:33,712
Never go past the

74
00:01:33,712 --> 00:01:34,400
woodpile.

75
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,656
Whatever's out there,

76
00:01:35,656 --> 00:01:36,628
we don't go looking

77
00:01:36,628 --> 00:01:37,275
for it.

78
00:01:38,474 --> 00:01:39,186
By noon,

79
00:01:39,186 --> 00:01:40,522
my head was pounding.

80
00:01:40,522 --> 00:01:41,358
June's too.

81
00:01:41,358 --> 00:01:42,236
I figured it was

82
00:01:42,236 --> 00:01:43,030
the Quiet.

83
00:01:43,030 --> 00:01:44,450
Pressure, like before a

84
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:45,036
storm.

85
00:01:45,936 --> 00:01:46,722
I went out for

86
00:01:46,722 --> 00:01:47,260
wood.

87
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,254
And the weird thing

88
00:01:48,254 --> 00:01:48,792
is...

89
00:01:48,792 --> 00:01:49,578
out there,

90
00:01:49,578 --> 00:01:50,653
by the woodpile,

91
00:01:50,653 --> 00:01:51,896
the headache just...

92
00:01:51,896 --> 00:01:52,474
faded.

93
00:01:52,474 --> 00:01:53,385
Like the cold was

94
00:01:53,385 --> 00:01:54,503
squeezing it out.

95
00:01:55,503 --> 00:01:56,414
Back inside,

96
00:01:56,414 --> 00:01:57,716
it came right back.

97
00:01:57,716 --> 00:01:58,975
That's how I knew.

98
00:01:58,975 --> 00:02:00,103
The Quiet was getting

99
00:02:00,103 --> 00:02:00,841
stronger.

100
00:02:02,941 --> 00:02:04,069
That afternoon,

101
00:02:04,069 --> 00:02:05,432
something in the kitchen

102
00:02:05,432 --> 00:02:06,653
started chirping.

103
00:02:06,653 --> 00:02:08,390
Grandpa's old smoke alarm,

104
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:09,847
screaming at nothing.

105
00:02:09,847 --> 00:02:11,443
There wasn't any smoke.

106
00:02:12,044 --> 00:02:12,774
So I took the

107
00:02:12,774 --> 00:02:13,788
batteries out...

108
00:02:13,788 --> 00:02:14,598
and put them in

109
00:02:14,598 --> 00:02:15,573
the flashlight.

110
00:02:15,573 --> 00:02:16,425
We were going to

111
00:02:16,425 --> 00:02:17,235
need light.

112
00:02:19,036 --> 00:02:19,907
Then the sun went

113
00:02:19,907 --> 00:02:20,424
down.

114
00:02:21,924 --> 00:02:22,788
June was the one

115
00:02:22,788 --> 00:02:24,021
who saw them first.

116
00:02:24,342 --> 00:02:24,804
Noah.

117
00:02:24,804 --> 00:02:26,010
Someone's in the trees.

118
00:02:27,411 --> 00:02:28,353
Two of them.

119
00:02:28,353 --> 00:02:29,508
Taller than any person

120
00:02:29,508 --> 00:02:30,193
I know.

121
00:02:30,193 --> 00:02:31,219
Each with one white

122
00:02:31,219 --> 00:02:31,818
eye...

123
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:33,016
that didn't blink.

124
00:02:34,917 --> 00:02:35,989
I wrote rule four

125
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:37,498
with a shaking hand.

126
00:02:37,498 --> 00:02:38,765
Never answer the Tall

127
00:02:38,765 --> 00:02:39,400
Ones.

128
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,509
They didn't move.

129
00:02:41,509 --> 00:02:42,557
They just watched.

130
00:02:42,557 --> 00:02:43,681
Then, together,

131
00:02:43,681 --> 00:02:44,543
they turned...

132
00:02:44,543 --> 00:02:45,515
and walked toward the

133
00:02:45,515 --> 00:02:46,039
cabin.

134
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:50,734
Three knocks.

135
00:02:50,734 --> 00:02:51,669
And rule five came

136
00:02:51,669 --> 00:02:52,278
to me,

137
00:02:52,278 --> 00:02:53,092
right then.

138
00:02:54,391 --> 00:02:54,794
Never.

139
00:02:54,794 --> 00:02:55,169
Open.

140
00:02:55,169 --> 00:02:55,514
The.

141
00:02:55,514 --> 00:02:55,889
Door.

142
00:02:57,489 --> 00:02:58,147
And then,

143
00:02:58,147 --> 00:02:59,026
from the other side

144
00:02:59,026 --> 00:02:59,906
of the door...

145
00:02:59,906 --> 00:03:01,151
something said my name.

146
00:03:02,251 --> 00:03:03,141
Noah?

